    'meta_description' => 'Prepare for the Nepal Nursing Council staff nurse licensing exam (NLEN): pattern, syllabus weightage, passing marks, and free mock test practice.',
    'intro' => 'The National Licensure Examination for Nurses (NLEN) is the Nepal Nursing Council\'s (NNC) licensing exam — passing it is mandatory for PCL Nursing and BSc Nursing graduates before they can register and practice as nurses in Nepal. Nepali citizens who studied nursing abroad, and eligible foreign nationals, also need to sit and pass it before working as a nurse in Nepal. Midwifery graduates sit a related exam, the National Licensure Examination for Midwives (NLEM), which adds a hands-on OSPE practical component alongside the written test.

